---
description: Explicit CMS CRUD requirements and language reference candidate
alwaysApply: true
---
Read docs/crud.md before adding a CRUD. Languages is a candidate awaiting user approval, not a final approved template. Follow the explicit requirements: empty HTML table shell, page-only Domi DataTable assets and JS entry, bounded server-side AJAX/sort/filter/pagination, first-column selection, last-column actions, filter drawer, real stats only, loading/error/animated empty states, sticky translated form actions, shared AJAX transport and loadingButton, accessible inline errors plus toast, dto/service/PackageCore contracts, safe documented hooks and relevant tests. Use Domi localization for PHP-managed toolbar keys. Save stays in place; explicit Save and new / Save and close may navigate only after success, as documented. Do not modify installation/login when implementing registry CRUDs.

Requested UI contract (visual approval pending): list toolbar has Add and an Actions dropdown (Help is always last). Search, filter and conditionally visible selection-review controls sit outside the table; pagination is below the table card. Keep selection by stable ID across AJAX pages, sorting and filters for the current document, never localStorage. Confirm all bulk operations in the shared accessible dialog with names/count; warn when none are selected. Block list controls and cover the table with a translucent loading overlay during requests. Form toolbar uses Cancel opposite a split Save button with Save and new / Save and close. Every list owns translated help content using common/crud/dialog. All visible labels, menus, alerts and help use Page::addLocalize; do not hardcode JS strings.

All product selects must use Select2 registered through Domi and enhanced by common/selects.js, with theme, direction, labels, focus and dialog dropdownParent support. Do not introduce plain native-only selects. The installer retains its existing specialized Select2 lifecycle. Read docs/localization.md: active language choices and direction come from the package language table; bootstrap config is only for pre-database installation. Do not hardcode en/fa choices in UI or validation.

Use shared backdrop dismissal for native dialogs and shared translated accordion headings (`crud.help_sections`) for page help. Keep title/actions aligned in one form header row, Cancel adjacent to split Save, and expose Edit on read-only views. Prefer existing JobMetric service methods for persistence; CMS adapters add only application policy, safe hooks and table contracts absent from the package. Render language flags from the package's published getFlags registry.

Editable CRUD forms use common/unsaved and reset the dirty baseline only after successful persistence. For change history reuse RecordHistory with an explicit public-field allowlist; write in the mutation transaction, skip no-ops, never log raw input or secrets, and paginate authenticated reads. See docs/crud.md for retention and deleted-record behavior.

Editable existing records must reject stale/missing optimistic versions before persistence hooks under the mutation lock. Return an explicit conflict without clearing drafts; replace the version only after a successful save. Never offer silent last-write-wins behavior.

Visual parity is mandatory: every new registry CRUD must copy the complete Languages CRUD markup, shared classes, button order, split-save dimensions/alignment, dropdown placement, dialogs, loading/empty/error states, selection behavior and responsive rules exactly. Only domain fields, labels and validation may differ; do not invent a second CRUD visual pattern.

Password controls are a shared application standard: use the security page's `cms-settings-control` + `cms-password-input` structure, toggle behavior, strength meter and guidance semantics wherever a CRUD edits passwords. Do not create per-page password control markup or styling.

All inputs and selects are shared controls: exactly one border belongs to the control wrapper, and nested password inputs are borderless. Reuse the established security/language control DOM and classes; page-specific border, padding, focus or wrapper variants are not allowed.

Render fields with the shared Blade components under `resources/views/components/form` (`x-form.field`, `x-form.input`, `x-form.select`, `x-form.textarea`, `x-form.password`) so labels, errors, accessibility attributes, and control markup stay consistent across every CMS form.

Every CMS page and state-changing endpoint must declare a registered Rolix permission at the route boundary. Direct URLs must return 403 when unauthorized, using the in-shell CMS access-denied presentation for HTML and a 403 JSON response for AJAX/API requests. Navigation, child menus, cards, buttons, and actions must be removed when their permission is unavailable; remove an entire parent menu when none of its children are authorized. UI hiding never replaces server-side enforcement. Use the shared `AdminAccess` decision service so route and presentation checks obey the same parent inheritance and explicit-deny precedence.

Archive workflow exception explicitly requested by the user: extension ZIP upload/upgrade forms automatically inspect on file selection/drop and expose a standalone placement-confirmation action only during review, with selection and review shown separately and Back returning within the same document. Do not add Save and new / Save and close to these archive forms. Archive failures render once inside the upload surface; do not duplicate them in external field summaries or error toasts. Plugin record forms retain the normal split-save toolbar and shared error handling. See docs/crud.md and docs/extensions.md.

Single-instance extension forms save in place. Save and close and Cancel return to the inventory (reopening the owner where applicable) using the server-supplied Domi URL. Validation failures remain on the form. Multiple-instance forms retain their instance-list return behavior.
